@page "/qview"

<PageTitle>QView - Collyn Brenner</PageTitle>

<ProjectsPageTemplate>
    <article class="project-info">
        <h1>QView</h1>
        <p class="project-meta">
            GitHub Branch:
            <a href="https://github.com/bnicholson/QViewNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">/bnicholson/QViewNG</a>
            (future: <a href="https://github.com/bnicholson/QView" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">/bnicholson/QView</a>)
        </p>

        <p>
            QView is a web app for running Bible quizzing tournaments, from the first registration to the final stats.
            Built by QuizStuff in partnership with NYI Youth Quizzing, QuizStuff.com and TeenBibleQuiz.com, it gives
            coaches, tournament managers and spectators one place to work. Anyone can follow a tournament and watch the
            action unfold, and a free account opens up features like registering teams and hosting tournaments.
        </p>
        <p>
            For coaches, QView cuts down on repetitive work. Quizzers are kept in reusable Rosters, which can be shared
            with other coaches, and the equipment a team brings is kept in reusable Gear Sets. Registering for a new
            tournament then means choosing what is already saved instead of entering it all again. Teams, gear and
            volunteers are all registered through the tournament's own page during the registration window its
            director sets.
        </p>
        <p>
            For tournament managers, QView covers the whole event: creating a tournament and its rooms, setting up
            divisions and registration, scheduling rounds and games, and setting the question types for each round. On
            tournament day, each room connects to QuizMachine so managers can monitor the rooms and resend game data
            when needed. Afterward, stats are computed with stats groups, and results can be imported and exported,
            including results carried over by hand from rooms that were not connected.
        </p>
        <p>
            QView stands on the shoulders of the software that came before it. It unifies two platforms plus several
            small features that, until now, have existed as separate pieces of software, each built with care by people
            who have served quizzing for years. QView seeks to build on their work rather than replace its spirit:
            bringing these pieces together means the data stored can be used in the greatest number of valuable
            features for users. It also aims to make that value easier to reach, especially for districts that have
            found setting up earlier tools to be more effort than they could give. The goal throughout is the benefit
            of the entire Teen Bible Quizzing ministry.
        </p>
    </article>
</ProjectsPageTemplate>

